# A one-clause widget whose parameter is a tuple pattern over a bundle, given a bundle
# that is a function's result, neither written out nor named (Semantics ch. 8: a widget's
# parameters are patterns, as a function's are; Type System ch. 2, "Bundles": a bundle is
# a plain aggregate, a value any expression may give). Written by Claude on the
# claude-lowering branch; subject to change.
emit Ui.*
test mod Tests
use Ui.*

Both: fn !Click, $Nat -> ((!Click, $Nat))
fn Both !tap, $count = ((!tap, $count))

@Counted: fn Text, ((!Click, $Nat)) -> @unit
fn @Counted name, ((!more, $guests)):
    $clicks <- 0 then $clicks + 1 on !more
    Ui.Label($text=$"{name}: {$guests} guests, {$clicks} clicks")

@main: @unit
@main:
    !more <- Ui.Button($label=$"more")                            # 0
    $guests <- 1 then $guests + 1 on !more
    @Counted "b", (Both !more, $guests)                           # 1
